(ry) and the HAIl/TALE/ALL REAL

Really great job in These two short verses

The said earthworms -both the shot out guts and literal worms craving for the corpse- get on him after killing his victim.



A possible interpretation that’s exclusive to the latter, would be considering Wayne’s rapper persona of being a martian, an out-of-here, combined to the “planet” interpretation of the “earth” mention ;
That in mind places him on an outer perspective from the mere human he’s shooting at his own earth/turf, and from the victim’s race/crew he’s belittling as earthworms — a species living in earth (the actual planet in this case). Thus the “shoot you in your earth” preposition use, instead of “on”, since earthworms (his victim’s race to him) live in earth and not on it.

Some wordplay:

A dentist would tell a patient to use dental floss every day of the week;

In street terms, to floss is to show off what you have, the more expensive stuff the better.

This hook is in the same style of Mike Jones' famous hook on the original song;

Back then they didn’t want, now I’m hot they all on me

A mac-10 is an intimidating gun.

Double entendre from Weezy here;

-Lowes is a luxury hotel in Miami. Wayne invited your girl there for “dinner”.

-it sounds like he is saying “invite your girl to my suite at the low, she left high” playing with the antonyms “low/high”. Meaning, Wayne invited your girlfriend behind your back, and she left the room with an emotion of euphoria (either sexual pleasure or under drug influence…or both)

Double entendre;
Lil Wayne is saying he squeezes him quicker than the wind breeze, meaning gasping for air. As he’s squeezing the trigger of a gun quicker than the “wind breeze”.

He’s says that he will leave the “thick cheese” full of bullet holes, hence the Swiss cheese. Which is full of holes.

“Mr. Carter” could refer to either Wayne or Jay-Z. Both rappers share the last name “Carter”;

Lil Wayne: Dwayne Michael Carter, Jr.

Jay-Z: Shawn Corey Carter
